"""STM32H725RGV6 - Arm Cortex-M7 MCU, 550 MHz, 1 MB flash, 564 KB RAM, VFQFPN68 8x8 mm.

Bare part: symbol, footprint and pins. Decoupling, the SMPS inductor, the reset
and boot straps and the clocks belong to the board.

Documents: DS13311 Rev 5 (datasheet), AN5419 Rev 3 (power supply hardware),
RM0468 (reference manual), ES0491 (errata: no item on the supply pins).

Package (DS13311 Table 8, VFQFPN68 SMPS column; Figure 4):
- VSS pads are connected to the exposed pad (Figure 4 note 2): pad 69 is VSS
  and joins GND here with every other VSS, VSSA and VSSSMPS pin.
- The VFQFPN68 variant is "DCDC only" (DS13311 page 1): there is no VDDLDO pin,
  so the core runs from the SMPS. VDD33USB, VDD50USB, VREF+/VREF- and PDR_ON
  are not bonded out (Table 8, no VFQFPN68 pin). VREF+/VREF- are internally
  connected to VDDA/VSSA when the pins are not available
  (Figures 46-47 note 1, page 202).
- The datasheet names the three core-supply pins VCAP; this package calls them
  VCAP1 (pad 33), VCAP2 (pad 49) and VCAP3 (pad 66), as AN5419 Figure 5 does,
  so each can be decoupled and checked on its own.

Supply ranges (DS13311 Table 13 "General operating conditions", page 116):
- VDD 1.62-3.6 V; VDDSMPS 1.62-3.6 V with VDDSMPS = VDD.
- VDDA 1.62-3.6 V when the ADC or comparators are used (DAC 1.8 V min, OPAMP
  2.0 V min; 0 V allowed only when no analog peripheral is used).
- VBAT 1.2-3.6 V (note 2: may drop to 0 V when VDD is present).
- VCORE with the internal regulator (SMPS) on: 0.95 V (VOS3) to 1.40 V (VOS0),
  page 117. VCAPx and VFBSMPS sit on VCORE in the Direct SMPS supply.
- USB FS (PA11/PA12, FT_u pins) needs its USB supply at 3.0-3.6 V (Table 13,
  VDD33USB "USB used").

Direct SMPS supply (AN5419 Figure 5, page 10; Table 2, pages 7-8), what the
board must provide:
- VDDSMPS = VDD, 10 uF (+ 100 nF / 10 uF / 4.7 uF options) at the pin.
- 2.2 uH inductor from VLXSMPS to VCORE, as close as possible to VLXSMPS;
  2 x 10 uF (ESR 5 mOhm) on the VFBSMPS side of the inductor. The 220 pF on
  VLXSMPS is for LQFP/BGA only.
- VFBSMPS and every VCAP pin on VCORE ("All VCAP connected together"), with
  100 nF close to each VCAP pin.
- VDD: 100 nF per pin plus one 4.7 uF. VDDA: 1 uF + 100 nF. VBAT: 1 uF +
  100 nF; VBAT tied to VDD when no backup supply is used.

Pin types (symbol): GPIOs bidirectional, NRST bidirectional (RST, embedded
pull-up), BOOT0 input, supplies and grounds power_in. VLXSMPS is power_out
(AN5419 Table 1, "Supply output"). The VCORE node needs exactly one power
output for KiCad ERC, and the inductor between VLXSMPS and VCORE is passive:
- VFBSMPS is typed power_out. It is the SMPS regulation point ("Supply
  regulation input", AN5419 Table 1): the net it sits on is the regulated
  VCORE, so it marks that net as driven by the on-chip SMPS.
- VCAP1-3 are typed power_in. In the Direct SMPS supply they take the core
  supply from VCORE ("Supply input/output", AN5419 Table 1; DS13311 Table 13).
  A VCAP pin left off VCORE is reported by ERC as an undriven power input, and
  three power outputs on one net would be a pin conflict.
"""

V_CORE = "0.95V to 1.40V"

VDD = io(Power(voltage="1.62V to 3.6V"))
VDDSMPS = io(Power(voltage="1.62V to 3.6V"))
VDDA = io(Power(voltage="1.62V to 3.6V"))
VBAT = io(Power(voltage="1.2V to 3.6V"))
# Switching node; AN5419 Table 2 gives its range as VCORE in the Direct SMPS supply.
VLXSMPS = io(Power(voltage=V_CORE))
VFBSMPS = io(Power(voltage=V_CORE))
VCAP1 = io(Power(voltage=V_CORE))
VCAP2 = io(Power(voltage=V_CORE))
VCAP3 = io(Power(voltage=V_CORE))
GND = io(Ground)

NRST = io(Net)
BOOT0 = io(Net)

PA0 = io(Net)
PA1 = io(Net)
PA2 = io(Net)
PA3 = io(Net)
PA4 = io(Net)
PA5 = io(Net)
PA6 = io(Net)
PA7 = io(Net)
PA8 = io(Net)
PA9 = io(Net)
PA10 = io(Net)
PA11 = io(Net)
PA12 = io(Net)
PA13 = io(Net)
PA14 = io(Net)
PA15 = io(Net)
PB0 = io(Net)
PB1 = io(Net)
PB2 = io(Net)
PB3 = io(Net)
PB4 = io(Net)
PB5 = io(Net)
PB6 = io(Net)
PB7 = io(Net)
PB8 = io(Net)
PB9 = io(Net)
PB10 = io(Net)
PB12 = io(Net)
PB13 = io(Net)
PB14 = io(Net)
PB15 = io(Net)
PC0 = io(Net)
PC1 = io(Net)
PC4 = io(Net)
PC5 = io(Net)
PC6 = io(Net)
PC7 = io(Net)
PC9 = io(Net)
PC10 = io(Net)
PC11 = io(Net)
PC12 = io(Net)
PC14 = io(Net)
PC15 = io(Net)
PD2 = io(Net)
PH0 = io(Net)
PH1 = io(Net)

# The exposed pad's stencil (TI SLUA271C 4.4: 50-70 % paste coverage on an exposed pad, in windows
# that let it outgas): "whole", one aperture as drawn; "split", windows round the thermal-via sites
# drawn on Cmts.User (0.2 mm), for vias left open in the pad.
Paste = enum("whole", "split")
paste = config(Paste, default="whole", help="the exposed pad's paste: one aperture, or windows round the thermal vias")
FOOTPRINT = {
    "whole": "QFN-68-1EP_8x8mm_P0.4mm_EP6.5x6.5mm.kicad_mod",
    "split": "QFN-68-1EP_8x8mm_P0.4mm_EP6.5x6.5mm_SplitPaste.kicad_mod",
}

Component(
    name="STM32H725RGV6",
    prefix="IC",
    symbol=Symbol(library="STM32H725RGV6.kicad_sym"),
    footprint=File(FOOTPRINT[paste.value]),
    part=Part(mpn="STM32H725RGV6", manufacturer="STMicroelectronics"),
    pins={
        "VBAT": VBAT,
        "VDD": VDD,
        "VDDSMPS": VDDSMPS,
        "VDDA": VDDA,
        "VLXSMPS": VLXSMPS,
        "VFBSMPS": VFBSMPS,
        "VCAP1": VCAP1,
        "VCAP2": VCAP2,
        "VCAP3": VCAP3,
        "VSS": GND,
        "VSSA": GND,
        "VSSSMPS": GND,
        "NRST": NRST,
        "BOOT0": BOOT0,
        "PA0": PA0,
        "PA1": PA1,
        "PA2": PA2,
        "PA3": PA3,
        "PA4": PA4,
        "PA5": PA5,
        "PA6": PA6,
        "PA7": PA7,
        "PA8": PA8,
        "PA9": PA9,
        "PA10": PA10,
        "PA11": PA11,
        "PA12": PA12,
        "PA13": PA13,
        "PA14": PA14,
        "PA15": PA15,
        "PB0": PB0,
        "PB1": PB1,
        "PB2": PB2,
        "PB3": PB3,
        "PB4": PB4,
        "PB5": PB5,
        "PB6": PB6,
        "PB7": PB7,
        "PB8": PB8,
        "PB9": PB9,
        "PB10": PB10,
        "PB12": PB12,
        "PB13": PB13,
        "PB14": PB14,
        "PB15": PB15,
        "PC0": PC0,
        "PC1": PC1,
        "PC4": PC4,
        "PC5": PC5,
        "PC6": PC6,
        "PC7": PC7,
        "PC9": PC9,
        "PC10": PC10,
        "PC11": PC11,
        "PC12": PC12,
        "PC14-OSC32_IN": PC14,
        "PC15-OSC32_OUT": PC15,
        "PD2": PD2,
        "PH0-OSC_IN": PH0,
        "PH1-OSC_OUT": PH1,
    },
)
